WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.034
Hire the most brilliant engineer alive.

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:05.948
Put them in a bad office, and we get bad work.

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:10.734
So where does an agent's quality come from? The hire, or the office?

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:18.588
An agent is a model plus a harness. The model is the hire. The harness is the office.

00:00:19.138 --> 00:00:23.263
LangChain froze the model and tuned only the harness.

00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:27.640
The score went from fifty-two point eight, to sixty-six point five.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:35.354
So we build the harness from the outside in. Containment. Guides. Sensors.

00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:36.236
Permissions.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:39.918
Each ring must hold when every ring inside it fails.

00:00:40.468 --> 00:00:46.013
Anthropic reports Claude Code users approve ninety-three percent of permission prompts.

00:00:46.063 --> 00:00:49.666
Three prompts a day get read. Thirty get clicked.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:57.183
In practice, we work the rings in order: walls, guides, sensors, permissions,

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:59.606
then one well-chosen hook.

00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:05.178
That's module four, the harness. Start with page one: The Office.
